==English==

===Etymology===
Attested since the 16th Century {{C.E.}}; from {{etyl|frm|en}} ''<span lang="frm">demoliss-</span>'', the stem of some conjugated forms of the verb {{term|demolir||to destroy”, “to tear down|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|dēmōlior||I tear down|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dəˈmɒl.ɪʃ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-demolish.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|demolish|es}}

# To [[destroy]]; to [[destruct]].
#: ''They '''demolished''' the old house and put up four townhouses.''
# {{context|transitive|figuratively|lang=en}} To utterly [[defeat]].
#* {{quote-news
|year=2011
|date=October 2
|author=Kevin Core
|title=Fulham 6 - 0 QPR
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/15051267.stm
|page=
|passage=Andrew Johnson scored a hat-trick as Fulham '''demolished''' London rivals Queens Park Rangers to win their Premier League fixture of the season.}}

